If an infant has a long-term-opioid-exposure then every clinician should observe the infant for at least 72 hours and should monitor the infant for a withdrawal-development.
If an infant has a long-term-opioid-exposure and has a buprenorphine-exposure then every clinician should observe the infant for at least 4 days.
If an infant has a long-term-opioid-exposure and has an ER-LA-opioid-exposure then every clinician should observe the infant for at least 4 days.
If an infant has a long-term-opioid-exposure and has a methadone-exposure then every clinician should observe the infant for at least 5 days.
